					"uidString" : "bNpls/1rQASwU6G7fp7/EA=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "Welcome to the second part! The first part stopped more or less where the first version of gt4carp stopped: a parser, a highlighter, a snippet, and a way to run code. In this part, we get to have some fun with what came after."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "/O40Kh7fQ9m3kRJjzGMK9A=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "Carp now has [Metacarp](https://github.com/cyberwitchery/metacarp), a compiler written in Carp whose phases are libraries and whose sessions can stay alive between inputs. That means our server can do a lot more than compile and run a cell. It can answer questions about our program: what type this is, what went wrong and where, what a macro expands to, what a project defines."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "ffFKLOLUSzWZgglAabX1Rg=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "In each of the following chapters, we take one of those answers, look at what the IDE does with it, and peek at the code that makes it happen. If you’d rather have the story than the tour, I wrote about it in [Carp in Glamorous Toolkit](https://blog.veitheller.de/Carp_in_Glamorous_Toolkit.html)."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "T1SJVYeSTXGr5W4h7t0bEA=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "A quick warning before we start: none of this is packaged yet. You have to build the server with Metacarp on your machine, as the [README](https://github.com/carpentry-org/gt4carp) describes, and GT looks for it where my checkout usually sits. Most snippets in these chapters need that server, but GT starts it on its own once it can find it."
			}
		]
	},
